---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@/config/site";

const lastUpdated = "1 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How JM Travels collects, uses and protects your personal information." noindex={false}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-jm max-w-3xl prose-copy space-y-6 text-body text-charcoal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-navy">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-body-s text-slate">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how {site.legalName} ("JM Travels", "we", "us") collects, uses, discloses and
        protects personal information when you use our website or contact us about our services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect information you provide directly to us, such as when you submit an enquiry, bespoke trip request, consultation request or referral, including:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>Name, email address, phone number and WhatsApp number</li>
        <li>Travel preferences, destinations, dates and budget information</li>
        <li>Any other information you choose to share with us in a message or form</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also collect limited technical information automatically, such as pages visited, referral source and
        general device/browser information, via analytics tools.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">How we use information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>To respond to enquiries and provide requested services</li>
        <li>To plan, coordinate and communicate about your trip</li>
        <li>To improve our website, services and content</li>
        <li>To understand which channels and content generate genuine interest</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Visa and travel documentation</h2>
      <p>
        Where visa assistance is requested, we may need to review certain travel documentation as part of that
        support. We only collect what is necessary for the specific service requested, and we do not request
        sensitive documents without a clear, specific business reason.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Sharing of information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We may share necessary details with third-party suppliers
        (hotels, transfer providers, activity operators, visa support partners) strictly to coordinate the travel
        services you have requested.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Data security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information, including secure
        form handling and restricted access to customer information. No method of transmission or storage is
        completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information by contacting us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="link-editorial">{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="link-editorial">{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="text-body-s text-slate pt-6 border-t border-mist">
        This policy is a general starting point and should be reviewed by a qualified professional for the specific
        jurisdictions in which JM Travels operates before relying on it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
